  "prefLabel": "Ins 3002.06 Privacy Notices to Group Policyholders",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-07-01",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3002.06 Privacy Notices to Group Policyholders. Unless a licensee is providing privacy notices directly to covered individuals described in Ins 3001.04 (f)(2)e.1., 2., or 3., a licensee shall provide initial, annual and revised notices to the plan sponsor, group or blanket insurance policyholder or group annuity contractholder, or workers’ compensation policyholder, in the manner described in Ins 3001.05 through Ins 3002.05, describing the licensee’s privacy practices with respect to nonpublic personal information about individuals covered under the policies, contracts or plans.\n\nSource. #7500, eff 7-1-01, EXPIRED: 7-1-09\n\nNew. #9922, eff 5-6-11; ss by #12749, eff 5-6-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3000.html"
